00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:01,007
Wait a minute.

523
00:19:01,007 --> 00:19:02,475
Were you just walking
on all fours?

524
00:19:02,475 --> 00:19:06,447
Look.

525
00:19:06,447 --> 00:19:09,048
Don’t you see anything?

526
00:19:09,048 --> 00:19:10,583
Like what?
There’s nothing to see.

527
00:19:10,583 --> 00:19:11,785
Right there.

528
00:19:11,785 --> 00:19:13,953
Water.
Source of all life.

529
00:19:13,953 --> 00:19:18,192
It’s wet.
Why?

530
00:19:18,192 --> 00:19:21,628
There’s nothing there.

531
00:19:21,628 --> 00:19:23,597
What’s the matter?

532
00:19:23,597 --> 00:19:25,565
Well, are you a feeb?

533
00:19:25,565 --> 00:19:27,367
Meg...

534
00:19:27,367 --> 00:19:29,435
I’ve gotta
get out of here.

535
00:19:29,435 --> 00:19:30,503
Right away.

536
00:19:30,503 --> 00:19:31,572
I need air.

537
00:19:31,572 --> 00:19:33,440
Meg.
Let’s elope.

538
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,508
We can catch a boat
to the main land, and...

539
00:19:35,508 --> 00:19:36,910
Be married this afternoon.

540
00:19:36,910 --> 00:19:38,078
What about the wedding?

541
00:19:38,078 --> 00:19:40,313
Look. I was never
for a big deal, anyway.

542
00:19:40,313 --> 00:19:42,182
I only agreed to it ’cause
you wanted it.

543
00:19:42,182 --> 00:19:44,183
Doesn’t it matter
that I still want it?

544
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:45,252
Please, meg.
Please.

545
00:19:45,252 --> 00:19:46,287
Do this for me.

546
00:19:46,287 --> 00:19:48,655
Just go away
with me right now.

547
00:19:48,655 --> 00:19:51,225
I told you.
That’s impossible.

548
00:19:51,225 --> 00:19:54,595
Plus, my mother and father
would think...

549
00:19:54,595 --> 00:19:56,062
Then i’ll have
to go by myself.

550
00:19:56,062 --> 00:19:57,397
Elope by yourself?

551
00:19:57,397 --> 00:20:01,335
What about the wedding?

552
00:20:01,335 --> 00:20:03,837
What about it,
meg?

553
00:20:03,837 --> 00:20:05,305
If you go,
there won’t be one.

554
00:20:05,305 --> 00:20:07,707
That’s all.

555
00:20:07,707 --> 00:20:08,775
Hmph. Elope by himself.

556
00:20:08,775 --> 00:20:09,843
Meg.

557
00:20:09,843 --> 00:20:10,910
What’s he gonna do?

558
00:20:10,910 --> 00:20:11,978
Carry himself
over the threshold?

559
00:20:11,978 --> 00:20:14,380
[Grumbles]
Men.

560
00:20:20,587 --> 00:20:24,190
Sam?

561
00:20:24,190 --> 00:20:25,825
Sessions presents--
david soul.

562
00:20:25,825 --> 00:20:27,427
♪ Don’t give
up on us ba-- ♪

563
00:20:27,427 --> 00:20:28,595
And now,
I will perform

564
00:20:28,595 --> 00:20:30,697
the greatest of all
magic accomplishments

565
00:20:30,697 --> 00:20:32,598
ever performed
on this island.

566
00:20:32,598 --> 00:20:33,733
The secret cabinet.

567
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:35,568
Don’t you have your
own family, kid?

568
00:20:35,568 --> 00:20:37,470
...the cabinet is empty.

569
00:20:37,470 --> 00:20:38,638
Tom.

570
00:20:38,638 --> 00:20:41,107
Tom. You’re not
paying any attention.

571
00:20:41,107 --> 00:20:42,375
Oh. I’m waitin’
for the waitress.

572
00:20:42,375 --> 00:20:44,678
Don’t you wanna see
the secret cabinet?

573
00:20:44,678 --> 00:20:46,813
Oh. Sure I do.
I-- I wouldn’t miss it.

574
00:20:46,813 --> 00:20:48,248
Go ahead.

575
00:20:48,248 --> 00:20:50,983
If I close the doors
to the magic cabinet,

576
00:20:50,983 --> 00:20:52,987
and say the magic words...

577
00:20:52,987 --> 00:20:54,788
And tap it with
my magic wand...

578
00:20:54,788 --> 00:20:57,490
Mm. I saw her
do this in vegas.

579
00:20:57,490 --> 00:20:58,925
Where’s my drink?

580
00:20:58,925 --> 00:21:03,030
It is now filled
with jelly beans.

581
00:21:03,030 --> 00:21:04,497
Tom stewart.

582
00:21:04,497 --> 00:21:06,165
Oh, firm-- huh?

583
00:21:06,165 --> 00:21:09,368
Fine one you are.

584
00:21:09,368 --> 00:21:11,738
Oh, sandy.

585
00:21:11,738 --> 00:21:13,140
Sandy.

586
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:15,308
If you hate me for
the rest of your life,

587
00:21:15,308 --> 00:21:16,577
I deserve it.

588
00:21:16,577 --> 00:21:18,845
I couldn’t hate you,
no matter what you did.

589
00:21:18,845 --> 00:21:19,980
I killed someone.

590
00:21:19,980 --> 00:21:21,213
I hate you.

591
00:21:21,213 --> 00:21:22,315
No matter what.

592
00:21:22,315 --> 00:21:24,217
Even like...
Fighting with your sister?

593
00:21:24,217 --> 00:21:25,718
Meg’s mad at me,
you know.

594
00:21:25,718 --> 00:21:26,953
She’ll get over it.

595
00:21:26,953 --> 00:21:28,722
Besides,
if she doesn’t,

596
00:21:28,722 --> 00:21:30,223
you’ll be free
to marry me.

597
00:21:30,223 --> 00:21:31,290
Hmm?

598
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,358
Okay.

599
00:21:32,358 --> 00:21:33,427
From now on...

600
00:21:33,427 --> 00:21:34,962
You’re the other
woman in my life.

601
00:21:34,962 --> 00:21:36,295
Put her down,
jerry lee.

602
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:37,363
[Laughter]

603
00:21:37,363 --> 00:21:38,432
Oh, we gotta go.

604
00:21:38,432 --> 00:21:39,498
You run along now.

605
00:21:39,498 --> 00:21:40,700
I’ve got some
practicing to do.

606
00:21:40,700 --> 00:21:41,935
I’ll clean up your
magic stuff.

607
00:21:41,935 --> 00:21:42,935
Bye.

608
00:21:42,935 --> 00:21:44,037
Bye, tom.

609
00:21:53,747 --> 00:21:55,082
Mm-hmm.

610
00:21:55,082 --> 00:21:56,617
But kennedy would’ve won
even without texas.

611
00:21:56,617 --> 00:21:57,850
He didn’t need johnson.

612
00:21:57,850 --> 00:21:59,652
True. True. But still,
it must’ve been nice

613
00:21:59,652 --> 00:22:00,753
- to win texas.
- Mm.

614
00:22:00,753 --> 00:22:02,288
It probably made
him feel real good.

615
00:22:02,288 --> 00:22:03,423
[Power tool whirs]

616
00:22:03,423 --> 00:22:04,692
Now,
what’s goin’ on up there?

617
00:22:04,692 --> 00:22:06,092
It’s me, joel.
I’m cleaning up.

618
00:22:06,092 --> 00:22:08,462
You guys left crunch berries
everywhere up here.

619
00:22:08,462 --> 00:22:10,530
Oh, that’s great. Uh...
Try to keep quiet, will ya?

620
00:22:10,530 --> 00:22:11,632
We’re talkin’ here.

621
00:22:11,632 --> 00:22:13,100
Oh, great.
You guys just relax

622
00:22:13,100 --> 00:22:14,667
while I clean
up your mess.

623
00:22:14,667 --> 00:22:15,735
- Okay.
- Great.

624
00:22:15,735 --> 00:22:17,203
Let us know if we can help.

625
00:22:17,203 --> 00:22:18,272
Anyway, servo.
Johnson shmohnson.

626
00:22:18,272 --> 00:22:19,405
You can’t say
that kennedy--

627
00:22:19,405 --> 00:22:21,475
- [joel screams]
- Whoa. Whoa.

628
00:22:21,475 --> 00:22:23,110
Joel.
What are you doing?

629
00:22:23,110 --> 00:22:24,778
Do you have any
self control at all?

630
00:22:24,778 --> 00:22:26,713
I fell. I’m hanging
here by one arm.

631
00:22:26,713 --> 00:22:28,215
You guys have to help me.

632
00:22:28,215 --> 00:22:29,282
Ah.

633
00:22:29,282 --> 00:22:30,550
Uh, tom?
Did you hear that?

634
00:22:30,550 --> 00:22:31,718
We have to help joel.

635
00:22:31,718 --> 00:22:33,087
Yeah.
As a general rule,

636
00:22:33,087 --> 00:22:35,155
I don’t like being told
what I have to do.

637
00:22:35,155 --> 00:22:36,723
Something about
it just gets to me.

638
00:22:36,723 --> 00:22:39,258
Yeah. Well, I guess the cat’s
on the other foot now, huh?

639
00:22:39,258 --> 00:22:40,593
[Laughter]

640
00:22:40,593 --> 00:22:42,428
Maybe we should at least
consider helping him though.

641
00:22:42,428 --> 00:22:44,097
Uh, he does owe
me two space credits.

642
00:22:44,097 --> 00:22:45,698
Oh, i’m willing
to consider it.

643
00:22:45,698 --> 00:22:46,967
[Laughs]

644
00:22:46,967 --> 00:22:48,435
Come on,
you guys.

645
00:22:48,435 --> 00:22:49,903
Uh, there may
be a few changes

646
00:22:49,903 --> 00:22:50,970
around here though,
joel.

647
00:22:50,970 --> 00:22:52,472
Um...
For instance--

648
00:22:52,472 --> 00:22:53,940
how late can
we stay up tonight?

649
00:22:53,940 --> 00:22:56,142
Uh, 8:30.
Same as always.

650
00:22:56,142 --> 00:22:57,210
Hmm.

651
00:22:57,210 --> 00:22:58,278
Oh. Okay.

652
00:22:58,278 --> 00:22:59,345
Joel.
Your arm getting tired?

653
00:22:59,345 --> 00:23:00,413
Okay. 9:00.

654
00:23:00,413 --> 00:23:05,118
[Laughter]

655
00:23:05,118 --> 00:23:06,553
Hey. Come on.

656
00:23:06,553 --> 00:23:07,720
You know, joel,

657
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:09,588
I think i’d like
to be taller than you,

658
00:23:09,588 --> 00:23:10,657
and more popular.

659
00:23:10,657 --> 00:23:12,125
Look at that.
What a pathetic figure.

660
00:23:12,125 --> 00:23:13,660
[Laughter]

661
00:23:13,660 --> 00:23:14,727
Oh, joel?

662
00:23:14,727 --> 00:23:15,795
What?

663
00:23:15,795 --> 00:23:17,563
I’m very sorry.
It’s just that

664
00:23:17,563 --> 00:23:19,232
you’ve put us in a rather
unusual situation.

665
00:23:19,232 --> 00:23:20,267
Mm-hmm.

666
00:23:20,267 --> 00:23:21,768
Uh... hey,
uh... okay.

667
00:23:21,768 --> 00:23:23,035
Let’s have
a nice smoked duck

668
00:23:23,035 --> 00:23:24,303
and goat cheese
pizza tonight, huh?

669
00:23:24,303 --> 00:23:25,372
- Mm.
- Oh, come on.

670
00:23:25,372 --> 00:23:27,173
You guys really
expect me to make that?

671
00:23:27,173 --> 00:23:29,108
No.
No, mr. Robinson.

672
00:23:29,108 --> 00:23:30,543
I expect you to die.

673
00:23:30,543 --> 00:23:31,845
[Laughter]

674
00:23:31,845 --> 00:23:33,780
Come on.
You have to help me.

675
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:35,382
Oh.
There he goes again.

676
00:23:35,382 --> 00:23:36,650
Boy,
that makes me angry.

677
00:23:36,650 --> 00:23:37,650
And hungry.

678
00:23:37,650 --> 00:23:38,752
Hey.
Let’s dig into

679
00:23:38,752 --> 00:23:40,287
those super mario
fruit chunks, okay?

680
00:23:40,287 --> 00:23:41,353
- Great idea.
- Yeah.

681
00:23:41,353 --> 00:23:42,822
We have a date
with mrs. Butterworth.

682
00:23:42,822 --> 00:23:44,623
Mm.
Sounds delicious.

683
00:23:51,632 --> 00:23:53,467
Oh, man.
I got an indian jumpsuit.

684
00:23:53,467 --> 00:23:55,735
[All]
Oh...

685
00:23:55,735 --> 00:23:56,803
Ugh.

686
00:23:56,803 --> 00:23:58,972
You have nice calves.

687
00:23:58,972 --> 00:24:00,807
Let’s see.
Um...

688
00:24:00,807 --> 00:24:04,643
[All hum chopsticks]

689
00:24:04,643 --> 00:24:06,378
♪♪ [Piano music]

690
00:24:06,378 --> 00:24:10,117
Oh, I feel so bad.

691
00:24:10,117 --> 00:24:12,285
♪ I’m gonna kill
me a girlfriend ♪

692
00:24:12,285 --> 00:24:13,353
♪ yes yes ♪

693
00:24:13,353 --> 00:24:15,588
♪ then marry
the girl I meet ♪

694
00:24:15,588 --> 00:24:16,957
Testify.

695
00:24:16,957 --> 00:24:18,858
♪ Gonna kill
me a girlfriend ♪

696
00:24:18,858 --> 00:24:20,360
♪ she’ll turn
into seaweed ♪

697
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:21,762
Mm-hmm.

698
00:24:21,762 --> 00:24:23,797
♪ It’s the blues
she’ll be wailin’ ♪

699
00:24:23,797 --> 00:24:26,667
♪ ’cause of my dirty deed ♪

700
00:24:26,667 --> 00:24:28,835
And that faulty
lighthouse railing, baby.

701
00:24:28,835 --> 00:24:30,003
- Oh.
- What is this?

702
00:24:30,003 --> 00:24:31,638
A better homes
and gardens video?

703
00:24:31,638 --> 00:24:32,705
Hmm.

704
00:24:32,705 --> 00:24:34,407
♪♪ [Piano]

705
00:24:34,407 --> 00:24:37,943
Ooh, baby.

706
00:24:37,943 --> 00:24:39,378
Hmm?

707
00:24:39,378 --> 00:24:42,248
[Female singing]

708
00:24:42,248 --> 00:24:45,018
Oh, suddenly he’s writing
a charles ives piece.

709
00:24:45,018 --> 00:24:47,687
♪ Lonely heart ♪

710
00:24:47,687 --> 00:24:49,522
There’s a pencil sharpener
on the end there.

711
00:24:49,522 --> 00:24:50,923
Why, it’s sessions.

712
00:24:50,923 --> 00:24:54,093
♪ I’m tormented ♪

713
00:24:54,093 --> 00:24:56,863
♪ by my love for you ♪

714
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:02,702
Milton bradley presents--
"tormented."

715
00:25:02,702 --> 00:25:04,503
Where you’re the killer.
Woman not included.

716
00:25:06,005 --> 00:25:07,240
Hey.

717
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:09,308
Huh.

718
00:25:09,308 --> 00:25:13,513
Wonder if this is on cd.

719
00:25:13,513 --> 00:25:15,282
Tormented.

720
00:25:15,282 --> 00:25:17,217
Now, it’s a coaster.
[Laughs]

721
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:24,757
Where was I?

722
00:25:24,757 --> 00:25:26,458
Hey.

723
00:25:26,458 --> 00:25:28,428
Now I do have the blues.

724
00:25:28,428 --> 00:25:31,898
[Female singing]

725
00:25:31,898 --> 00:25:33,165
Now,
cut that out.

726
00:25:33,165 --> 00:25:34,833
♪ I am-- ♪

727
00:25:34,833 --> 00:25:36,402
Huh?

728
00:25:36,402 --> 00:25:39,772
♪ The memories ♪

729
00:25:39,772 --> 00:25:43,977
All right.
Allen funt, where are you?

730
00:25:43,977 --> 00:25:45,045
Oops.

731
00:25:45,045 --> 00:25:46,580
Aw, cripes.
I just remembered.

732
00:25:46,580 --> 00:25:48,515
I borrowed this
from the library.

733
00:25:50,883 --> 00:25:55,488
[Intermittent tapping]

734
00:25:55,488 --> 00:25:56,555
Hmm?

735
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:58,792
Who’s there?

736
00:25:58,792 --> 00:26:00,493
It’s mrs. Ellis,
tom.

737
00:26:00,493 --> 00:26:02,162
[Gasps]

738
00:26:02,162 --> 00:26:06,667
Uh, hiya, mr. B.

739
00:26:06,667 --> 00:26:09,235
Hey, it’s,
uh, blind lemon pledge.

740
00:26:09,235 --> 00:26:11,070
I brought you
some flowers.

741
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:13,172
Uh, yeah. Just put that
in the goldfish bowl.

742
00:26:13,172 --> 00:26:16,008
Something the matter,
tom?

743
00:26:16,008 --> 00:26:17,777
What makes you say that?

744
00:26:17,777 --> 00:26:19,745
You sound upset.

745
00:26:19,745 --> 00:26:21,480
Perhaps i’d better
check you another time.

746
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:23,417
Oh, no.
No, mrs. Ellis.

747
00:26:23,417 --> 00:26:26,285
No. Come in.
Sit down.

748
00:26:26,285 --> 00:26:27,820
Thank you for the flowers.
They’re lovely.

749
00:26:27,820 --> 00:26:29,788
Watch out, mr. Buckalew.
Watch out, honey.

750
00:26:29,788 --> 00:26:31,590
Look out.

751
00:26:33,460 --> 00:26:35,028
Mrs. Ellis...

752
00:26:35,028 --> 00:26:36,228
I want to ask
you something.

753
00:26:36,228 --> 00:26:37,630
How many fingers
am I holding up?

754
00:26:37,630 --> 00:26:38,698
Stop it.

755
00:26:38,698 --> 00:26:40,333
It sounds kind of silly,
but...

756
00:26:40,333 --> 00:26:42,735
Well, do you believe that
the spirits of the dead

757
00:26:42,735 --> 00:26:45,072
can come back
to haunt the living?

758
00:26:45,072 --> 00:26:47,007
Do you believe in ghosts?

759
00:26:47,007 --> 00:26:48,273
Do you believe
in peanut butter?

760
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:50,177
What makes you ask
a thing like that?

761
00:26:50,177 --> 00:26:52,212
You haven’t answered,
mrs. Ellis.

762
00:26:52,212 --> 00:26:54,813
Nobody believes
in ghosts nowadays.

763
00:26:54,813 --> 00:26:56,482
Do you?

764
00:26:56,482 --> 00:26:58,918
If anybody was
to ask me seriously,

765
00:26:58,918 --> 00:27:00,453
I would have to say no.

766
00:27:00,453 --> 00:27:02,588
What if I asked you
dressed in a clown suit?

767
00:27:02,588 --> 00:27:04,723
A real estate agent runs
into many strange things

768
00:27:04,723 --> 00:27:06,727
in an empty house
sometimes.

769
00:27:06,727 --> 00:27:07,927
What kind of things?

770
00:27:07,927 --> 00:27:11,597
Well, there was
a family named samuels.

771
00:27:11,597 --> 00:27:13,433
They lived in that
last house down the beach.

772
00:27:13,433 --> 00:27:14,767
On the left?

773
00:27:14,767 --> 00:27:16,168
One day,
their little boy

774
00:27:16,168 --> 00:27:18,838
took his dog
and went fishing.

775
00:27:18,838 --> 00:27:20,173
They never came back.

776
00:27:20,173 --> 00:27:21,908
And nobody knows
what happened to them.

777
00:27:21,908 --> 00:27:23,075
Coincidence?
Read the book.

778
00:27:23,075 --> 00:27:25,245
After the samuels’
moved away,

779
00:27:25,245 --> 00:27:29,448
I signed three tenants
during that first month...

780
00:27:29,448 --> 00:27:32,218
But not one of them would
stay more than a few days.

781
00:27:32,218 --> 00:27:34,487
Believe it or not.

782
00:27:34,487 --> 00:27:35,955
That doesn’t
prove anything.

783
00:27:35,955 --> 00:27:38,925
They complained
about an unseen dog,

784
00:27:38,925 --> 00:27:41,060
whining and scratching
at the door.

785
00:27:41,060 --> 00:27:43,062
But that wasn’t what made
them break their lease.

786
00:27:43,062 --> 00:27:45,232
The dog piddled the carpet
